    "title": "Pendulum: kinetic and potential energy exchange",
    "subject": "Physics",
    "topic": "Pendulum Energy",
    "objective": "Show kinetic and potential energy exchanging during a pendulum swing.",
    "learner": "Knows energy conservation.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "Both energies are maximum at the bottom",
      "Energy disappears"
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": "Without damping, KE + PE is constant: PE is largest at the turning points where the bob is highest and momentarily at rest, KE is largest at the lowest point where PE is zero, and the stacked bar keeps the same total height throughout."
  },
